            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="d6-01" n="1" xml:id="d6-01"/>

                <head>6. Airgram A–7576 From the Department of State to All Diplomatic Posts<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d6-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d6-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1973-09-04"
                        >September 4, 1973</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>LOS: July/August Session of the UN Seabed Committee</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached is the U.S. Delegation report on the summer session of the Seabed
                    Committee which is preparing for the Third U.N. Law of the Sea Conference. Since
                    we are now approaching the Conference itself, we expect increased interest in
                    these issues by host governments and an increased U.S. policy effort with many
                    of those governments. This report, consequently, furnishes important background
                    material for LOS officers.</p>
                <closer><signed> RUSH, ACTING</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d6-a1.xml" xpointer="d6-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–1973, POL 33–8, 9–17–73.
                    Confidential. Drafted by Leitzell; cleared by Stevenson, S/FW–COA, L/OA, JCS,
                    Defense, Interior, NOAA, NSF, CEQ, Treasury, and the Coast Guard; and approved
                    by Moore. A copy was sent to Hong Kong.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d6-f2" n="2" xml:id="d6-f2-content">
                <p>Acting Secretary Rush forwarded the final report of the U.S. Delegation to the
                    July/August 1973 Seabed Committee Session, which also acted as a preparatory
                    conference for the UNCLOS III.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
